# gateway.env.example
# Institutional AI gateway + MCP calendar producer, both halves on.
#
# Copy to <name>.env in this directory, fill in your institution's values, and
# run:  ./install.sh --profile <name>
#
# This is the shape of a profile for an adopter who already has (a) an AI
# gateway that speaks the Anthropic Messages API and (b) an MCP calendar
# connector their tenant has approved — i.e. someone inside an organization
# that has already made those choices, rather than an individual starting from
# a personal Anthropic key.
#
# NEVER put an API key in this file. It names the secret; the installer prompts
# for the value and stores it in the Keychain. See README.md in this directory
# for every key and what it does.

PROFILE_DESCRIPTION="Institutional AI gateway + MCP calendar pipeline"

# ---- Where Claude calls go --------------------------------------------------
# Non-secret config, not credentials: an endpoint, and the NAME of the secret
# that opens it. 20-secrets persists these two to ~/dev/secrets/.env and
# prompts separately for the key, whose VALUE goes to the platform keystore
# (macOS Keychain) and never into a file.
#
# They have to be persisted rather than exported because the LaunchAgents that
# run the tagger, voice-cleanup, and classifier on a schedule start from a bare
# environment — launchd does not source your shell.
LLM_BASE_URL="https://api.ai.example.edu"
LLM_API_KEY_NAME="EXAMPLE_AI_API_KEY"
LLM_GATEWAY_HELP_URL="https://it.example.edu/ai/api-access"

# Gateways sometimes expose aliases rather than dated Anthropic model ids, and
# sometimes strip the prompt-cache field. Leave both unset if yours behaves
# like the stock API.
# TAGGER_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"
# TAGGER_PROMPT_CACHE=1
# The nightly data-classification agent has its own pair (it wants a stronger
# model than the tagger, since a wrong tier is a disclosure risk).
# CLASSIFIER_MODEL="claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929"
# CLASSIFIER_PROMPT_CACHE=1

# ---- Opt-in components ------------------------------------------------------
# 52 and 54 are the two halves of one pipeline; run both or neither.
PROFILE_MEETING_PREPOPULATE=1
PROFILE_MEETING_PULL=1
PROFILE_DASHBOARD_ACTIONS=1

# ---- Answers to the prompts those components ask ----------------------------
# Left blank on purpose: per-person, and the installer will ask.
# PROFILE_DISPLAY_NAME=""
# PROFILE_EMAIL=""
# PROFILE_ADMIN_EMAILS=""

PROFILE_TENANT="example.edu"
# Every internal domain, not just the primary one. A university and its
# hospital on separate domains will otherwise have half its own people
# classified as external.
PROFILE_TENANT_DOMAINS="example.edu,med.example.edu"
PROFILE_TIMEZONE="America/New_York"

# Tool names as `claude mcp list` reports them — NOT as a desktop client
# labels them. Wrong prefix here is the most common reason a first run
# produces nothing and looks like a permissions problem.
PROFILE_MCP_PREFIX="mcp__claude_ai_Microsoft_365"
PROFILE_SEARCH_TOOL="outlook_calendar_search"
PROFILE_READ_TOOL="read_resource"

# Drop folder: producer writes here, consumer watches it. Default is
# ~/MeetingIngest (outside the vault so handoff files never sync or index).
# PROFILE_OUT_DIR="$HOME/MeetingIngest"
